1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
The ice hauling ship Canterbury is en route from Saturn's rings to Ceres when it encounters a distress signal.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Five members of the Canterbury's crew are dispatched in a shuttle to investigate: executive officer James "Jim" Holden, chief engineer Naomi Nagata, pilot Alex Kamal, engineer Amos Burton, and medic Shed Garvey.

3
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:53,000
They discover an abandoned transport vessel called the Scopuli, and find that the distress beacon which lured them is fake and contains Martian technology.

4
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:06,000
An unknown stealth warship arrives and, without warning, destroys the Canterbury with nuclear weaponry.

5
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Holden broadcasts a message out to the entire solar system implicating Mars in the destruction of the Canterbury, starting a war between Mars and the Belt.

6
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:50,000
The survivors of the Canterbury are ordered to rendezvous with the Martian battleship Donnager.

7
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:59,000
The ship's captain denies any knowledge of Martian involvement in the attack on the Canterbury.

8
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:03,000
The Donnager is attacked by unknown ships and destroyed.

9
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:12,000
While Holden and most of his crew manage to escape on a Martian frigate, Shed is killed.

10
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:21,000
The Canterbury's surviving crew flee to the protection of the OPA's leader, Colonel Fred Johnson.

11
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Analysis of a data chip recovered from the Donnager reveals that the mysterious stealth ships were built by Earth.

12
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Holden makes another public broadcast sharing this information, hoping to ease the tensions created by his prior implication of Mars.

13
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:55,000
This massively backfires, instead drawing Earth into the war.

14
00:03:55,000 --> 00:04:10,000
The Martian frigate Holden's crew escaped on is renamed the Rocinante and on it, Holden is sent to Eros Station to find an OPA operative who sent out a distress signal.

15
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:39,000
On Ceres Station, detective Joe Miller is illicitly contracted to locate Julie Mao, the daughter of very wealthy Lunar citizens, and send her back to her family against her will.

16
00:05:52,000 --> 00:06:05,000
Miller is warned both by his superiors and OPA operatives to stop looking into her disappearance, and is fired when he refuses.

17
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:39,000
Miller discovers that Mao had been involved with the OPA and was aboard the Scopuli when it disappeared.

18
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:55,000
Realizing that Mao's disappearance is connected to the destruction of the Canterbury, he travels to Eros to meet Holden and the crew of the Rocinante.

19
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:19,000
On Eros, Miller finds Holden's crew and helps them survive an ambush attempt.

20
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:27,000
They locate the body of Julie Mao in a hotel shower infected with a strange, organic growth.

21
00:07:38,000 --> 00:08:00,000
On her phone Miller finds logs detailing the progression of her affliction, which seems to be fueled by exposure to energy and radiation, and the coordinates of an asteroid where one of the ships that attacked the Canterbury is docked.

22
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:26,000
Before Miller and the crew of the Rocinante can leave Eros, a station-wide radiation alert is issued and security begins herding people into the numerous radiation shelters.

23
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:45,000
Miller and Holden discover that the radiation alert has been faked by Eros's security contractor, the Earth-based company Protogen, and that people in the shelters have in fact been infected with the same disease as Julie.

24
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:54,000
The zombie-like infected people attack the rest of Eros, spreading the infection via vomit.

25
00:08:54,000 --> 00:09:01,000
Miller and the crew of the Rocinante narrowly manage to escape the station.

26
00:09:52,000 --> 00:10:02,000
Miller and the crew of the Rocinante follow the coordinates from Julie's phone to find one of the stealth ships abandoned.

27
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:44,000
The team finds a Protogen video explaining that the organism is a biological replication mechanism created by extrasolar aliens with the intent of reaching Earth and hijacking its early biosphere in order to create something for its own mysterious purposes, but which had been captured by Saturn's gravity and stranded.

28
00:10:49,000 --> 00:11:11,000
Protogen, which had discovered the organism on Saturn's moon Phoebe and dubbed it the "protomolecule," orchestrated its release on Eros as an experiment in an attempt to discover what it was designed to do given a rich biological source.

29
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:45,000
To this end they had carried out the false flag attack on the Canterbury in order to start a war which would distract the Solar System from the criminal operation on Eros.

30
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:15,000
With the OPA, Miller and the crew of the Rocinante attack Protogen's secret base in the belt.

31
00:12:53,000 --> 00:13:13,000
They capture lead scientist Antony Dresden, who reveals he believes the Protomolecule is humanity's key to the stars, and that by modifying it for their purposes, humanity could become gods.

32
00:13:16,000 --> 00:14:09,000
Realizing that Dresden's rationale is likely to be accepted by the powers that be on Earth and Mars, and thus that this horrific research would allowed to continue, Miller summarily executes Dresden without warning, angering Holden.

33
00:14:57,000 --> 00:15:15,000
Realizing that it is likely that the Protomolecule will be sought after by malicious actors in the future, the OPA and Miller plans to crash a large ship into Eros to propel it into the Sun.

34
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:34,000
Miller leads a team onto the exterior of Eros to rig the station with bombs to ensure no one can capture it while en route.

35
00:15:53,000 --> 00:16:01,000
Miller, deciding he has completed everything he wanted in life, stays behind on Eros.

36
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:12,000
Just before the ship impacts the station, however, the trajectory of Eros is suddenly and inexplicably altered.

37
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:18,000
The Protomolecule proves to have an advanced method of spaceflight which negates both g-force and inertia.

38
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:28,000
Eros, being driven by this inexplicable force, sets off on a collision course with Earth at a speed that no human-made ship can match.

39
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:03,000
Miller, still on Eros, takes one of the bombs into the station in an attempt to destroy its maneuvering capabilities.

40
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:12,000
However, he realizes that Eros is being guided by Julie Mao, whose infected body is in a symbiotic relationship with the protomolecule.

41
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:38,000
Although she is being used by the Protomolecule, she retains enough agency for Miller to convince her to direct Eros away from Earth.

42
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:51,000
The station instead crashes into Venus, presumably killing both Miller and Mao.

43
00:17:51,000 --> 00:18:01,000
On Venus's surface, the Protomolecule promptly begins assembling a vast, mysterious structure.
